Both runs are gen_test_irq_basic at seed 165313640 and both carry THE SAME PROGRAM IMAGE,
+gen_mem_image_crc32=03c84170 +gen_mem_image_words=217, so the two waveforms are the same experiment
with one variable changed.

The window is the one rtl-arch's pair record names: dv/auto_dv/evidence/gen_ibus_props_irq_signature_reading.md
Section 3 gives sva_ibus_gnt_only_with_req at 18338500 (cycle 18334) for this seed, and the committed run
here fires at 183385000 ps, the same tick. The clock's posedges in this window are at ...500 and its
negedges at ...000.

1. COMMITTED DRIVER, transitions in 18336000..18342000

  clk        13 transitions, every 500
  req        18338000 -> 0    18338500 -> 1
  gnt        NO TRANSITION in the window
  rvalid     no transition
  outstanding 18338500 -> 3

  sampled at 183382ns, inside the low window and before the accepting posedge:
  clk=0  req=0  gnt=1  outstanding=4

  So the core withdrew its request for one half cycle, from the negedge at 18338000 to the posedge at
  18338500, and the grant STOOD THROUGH IT. The pre-edge sample of the accepting posedge is req=0 with
  gnt=1, which is what the property samples and what it reports.

2. REPAIRED DRIVER, the identical window

  clk        13 transitions, every 500
  req        18338000 -> 0    18338500 -> 1        (identical to the committed run)
  gnt_ready  18338500 -> 0    18339000 -> 1
  gnt        18338000 -> 0    18339000 -> 1
  rvalid     no transition
  outstanding 18338500 -> 3                        (identical)

  sampled at 183382ns, the same instant as above:
  clk=0  req=0  gnt_ready=1  gnt=0  outstanding=4

  The DRIVER'S DECISION IS THE SAME in both runs: gnt_ready is high through the low window, which is the
  falling-edge decision the committed driver made too. What differs is the gate. gnt tracks req down at
  18338000, so the pre-edge sample of the accepting posedge is req=0 with gnt=0 and the property has
  nothing to report. The driver then reads vif.gnt at that posedge, sees 0, counts a withdrawal, drops
  gnt_ready in the same time step, and enqueues nothing. It re-arms at the next negedge, 18339000, where
  req is live again and the grant is real.

3. THE REGION ORDERING, which is why the driver and the property cannot disagree

  req rises again AT the accepting posedge, 18338500. That does not race the driver's read, and the
  waveform shows why: gnt does not rise at 18338500 with it, it rises at 18339000. instr_req_o is
  combinational out of registers that update in the NBA region of that edge, so the core's reaction to
  the edge lands strictly after the driver's Active-region read. The driver therefore reads the gate
  computed from the PRE-EDGE request, which is exactly the value the property's Preponed sample uses.
  The two look at the same instant of the same signals by construction.

  The same ordering covers the opposite case: a request live in the pre-edge sample that falls because
  of the edge. There the driver reads gnt=1 and enqueues, and the property samples req=1 and gnt=1 and
  holds. Both are right, and they agree.

4. WHAT THIS PAIR DOES NOT SHOW

  One window on one seed. It shows the mechanism of the firing and the mechanism of its removal; the
  claim that no firing survives anywhere in either run is the property's own count in the run logs
  (one in the committed run, zero in the repaired one), not this read.
